# Move the ESP-NOW link off channel 3.
#
# TEC-NATKIT-50's evidence says the fault on this bench is a SHARED, EXTERNAL,
# TIME-VARYING receive impairment near channel 3: four leaves' beacon loss
# correlated at r = +0.67..+0.97, it switched off for all four in the same
# instant, and the wanted signal did not move by more than 2 dB while loss went
# from 65% to 0.1%. Signal flat with loss changing is the noise floor moving.
#
# ⚠️ APPLIES TO BOTH ENDS. A channel is not a per-node setting -- the primary and
# every leaf must be built with the same one or there is no link. That is why this
# is its own profile rather than a line in bench.defaults, which is leaves-only:
#
#     NATKIT_PROFILE=bench,ch10 ./build-role.sh leaf esp32       # leaves
#     NATKIT_PROFILE=ch10       ./build-role.sh primary esp32s3  # hub
#
# ⚠️ Channel 1 is NOT an alternative: a 25 MHz crystal's 96th and 97th harmonics
# land in it, which is a fault this rig has already had. 10 was measured at
# -22/-23 dBm and carried full rate historically.
#
# ⚠️ AND THIS IS AN EXPERIMENT, NOT A NEW DEFAULT. sdkconfig.defaults still says
# 3. If the soak on 10 is decisively better, move the default there and delete
# this file rather than leaving two answers in the tree.
CONFIG_NATKIT_ESPNOW_CHANNEL=10
